  {The energy loss per unit length in the STAR TPC.  The magnetic field was 0.25T.\cite{NIMSTARTPC}
  \label{TPCdEdx}}
\end{figure}

Need to add more discussion of energy loss.

Restrictions on the energy loss per unit length (dE/dx) in the STAR TPC were also applied.  The distribution of the measured dE/dx versus the reconstructed track \pT is plotted in \Fref{TPCdEdx}.  Clear bands are seen for \pion, K, p, deutrons and helium.  The dE/dx of daughter tracks can be used to reduce the background.  The number of standard deviations away from the center of the band is calculated and a 3$\sigma$ cut was applied by default.  \Fref{V0NSigmaExamples} shows the distributions of the number of $\sigma$ away from the center of the dE/dx band for the daughters for \lam candidates.  This cut is more effective at lower momenta, since the bands from different particles begin to merge above 1 \GeV in the STAR TPC.  At higher momenta, the bands begin to separate so then some resolution is possible.  It is also more effective for the p and \antiproton daughters of the \lam and \alam since there are more pions than protons produced \cite{IordanovaWWND08}.

